From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amaral Driver Lab <rickamaral94@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tu: reference the bound program state instead of copying it

tu_CmdBindPipeline copied the whole tu_program_state (about 10 KB: the
const state of every stage plus the shader hashes) into the command
buffer state on every graphics pipeline bind. A Turnip profile of a
draw-heavy title (about 2,000 binds per frame) showed that memcpy at
about 4% of the recording thread's samples.

Point at the pipeline's program state instead. Every reader runs while
recording a draw, after a pipeline was bound, and the pipeline has to
outlive the commands that use it, as it already does for the shaders
in cmd->state.shaders. The draw tracepoint copies the shader hashes
with strcpy, so it keeps no pointer into the state.

The descriptor-set bind paths read uses_bindless_base_addrs (Mesa
88b01a7c269), which can run before any pipeline is bound; a NULL
program there means "not used", as the zeroed copy did before.

Generated-by: LLM
